# The wallet this dashboard tracks. Defaults to the original wallet in code if unset;
# override to reuse this app for a different address.
WALLET_ADDRESS=0x89aC35e57216A51Cf08f1c14B3Ce19D6813ee492

# NodeReal MegaNode API key (dashboard.nodereal.io, free tier for BNB Chain). Used for native BNB
# + BEP-20 balances and transaction history on BSC via the BSCTrace JSON-RPC API
# (eth_getBalance + nr_getAssetTransfers) - BNB Chain's own endorsed replacement for the
# deprecated BscScan API. Moralis previously served this role but its free BSC tier ended
# 2026-09-01; Etherscan's unified V2 API doesn't offer a free tier for BNB Chain either, so
# NodeReal is the one free option left as of this writing. See src/lib/networks/nodeRealApi.ts
# for a caveat: its response shape for nr_getAssetTransfers isn't fully documented publicly, so
# that client validates the shape defensively and fails loudly (isolated to the BSC tab) rather
# than risk silently-wrong numbers if NodeReal's actual response differs from what's assumed.
NODEREAL_API_KEY=

# Etherscan API key (etherscan.io/apis, free tier). As of Etherscan's 2025 API v2 unification,
# ONE Etherscan-issued key covers Ethereum Mainnet AND Arbitrum One (selected via a `chainid`
# param) - there's no separate Arbiscan key/domain anymore. Used for native ETH + ERC-20 balances
# (derived by summing transfer history - the free tier has no bulk "all balances" endpoint) and
# transaction history on both networks. Free tier is one shared budget across both chains, not
# per-chain - budget accordingly if this wallet is very active on both.
ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=

# Hyperliquid needs no API key - src/lib/networks/hyperliquid.ts hits its public, keyless
# https://api.hyperliquid.xyz/info REST API for HyperCore (spot + perps), and a public HyperEVM
# JSON-RPC endpoint for the native HYPE balance only (no ERC-20 token discovery there without an
# indexer - see README's Known Limitations).

# Optional. CoinGecko free "Demo" API key (coingecko.com/en/api/pricing). Works without one
# at low request volume, but a key raises your rate limit. Used for current + historical USD
# pricing on every EVM network (BSC/Ethereum/Arbitrum) - none of their balance/history APIs
# attach live pricing themselves. Hyperliquid spot pricing comes from Hyperliquid's own API
# instead (CoinGecko can't resolve HyperCore assets by contract address).
COINGECKO_API_KEY=

# Upstash Redis (or the Vercel KV integration, which sets the same variable names) - backs
# the server-side response cache so the manual refresh button and every upstream API's rate
# limits behave in production. Local dev works without these; caching is just skipped.
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
